-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

IEEE 13, 34 and 123 node test feeders (tests/fixtures/feeders/)
  OpenDSS versions of the IEEE PES Distribution Test Feeders, as distributed in the OpenDSS repository
  (Distrib/IEEETestCases) under its BSD-3-Clause license; the files carry no license of their own.
  Feeder data: IEEE PES Distribution System Analysis Subcommittee, https://cmte.ieee.org/pes-testfeeders/

NREL SMART-DS (downloaded at run time by `load smartds`; not distributed)
  National Renewable Energy Laboratory, "SMART-DS Synthetic Electrical Network Data OpenDSS Models".
  CC-BY-4.0. https://data.openei.org/submissions/2981

HIFLD-schema mirrors (downloaded at run time by `load hifld`; not distributed)
  U.S. Electric Power Transmission Lines (HIFLD, archive), U.S. Government data hosted by Esri's
  Federal_User_Community under the Esri Master License Agreement.
  https://services2.arcgis.com/FiaPA4ga0iQKduv3/arcgis/rest/services/US_Electric_Power_Transmission_Lines/FeatureServer/0
  Electric Substations Southern California Clip (Robert Redford Conservancy, Pitzer College; sources SCAG, USGS,
  CEC, CALGEM). CC-BY-SA-4.0.
  https://services.arcgis.com/hVnyNvwbpFFPDV5j/arcgis/rest/services/CA_Substations_Final/FeatureServer/16

tests/fixtures/pecan_sample.csv is synthetic data in the Pecan Street Dataport export format. No Pecan Street data
is distributed; `loaders/pecan.py` reads the user's own export.
